  "id": "standardization",
  "term": "standardization",
  "definition": "Standardization is the process of making an assessment method uniform and objective so results can be interpreted more consistently across studies and clinical settings. In this context, it means using common procedures for balance-control testing to reduce methodological differences and support wider clinical use.",
